<title>USA: U S West rate cut delayed by court.</title>
<headline>U S West rate cut delayed by court.</headline>
<dateline>SALEM, Ore. 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U S West Communications Group said on Thursday that the Oregon Circuit Court for the County of Mario granted the firm's request for a stay of the state's May 19 order requiring the company to cut rates and refund $102 million retroactively.</p>
<p>The delay is pending a full review of the Oregon Public Utility Commission's May 19 order for U S West to cut rates by $97 million and pay the refund, U S West said in a statement.</p>
<p>The court scheduled to review the case in December 1997, U S West said.</p>
</text>
